1:# Ramses Auto Shutdown (Pisonet App)
4:The Ramses Auto Shutdown is an Electron desktop application designed for pisonet (coin-operated PC rental) businesses. It provides a custom login interface for members, integrates with a MikroTik hotspot portal for session management, and supports coin-insertion functionality via a JuanFi NodeMCU vendo. The application aims to provide a robust, secure, and user-friendly experience for pisonet users while offering an admin panel for kiosk configuration and detailed coin log management. It is designed to be deployed in environments ranging from standard desktop PCs to diskless/deep-freeze setups, with features like auto-shutdown, system hardening, and remote coin log synchronization. The project seeks to streamline pisonet operations, enhance user experience, and provide valuable business insights through its comprehensive logging and analytics.
35:- **App Role System:** Distinguishes between `auto-shutdown` (client) and `points` (server-only) roles using `RAMSES_APP_ROLE` environment variable, leading to separate settings files (`settings-client.json`, `settings-server.json`) and different default ports.
36:- **Rates Synchronization:** Auto-shutdown clients fetch and periodically sync coin/point rates from the Ramses Points server when configured.
38:- **Self-Arming Watchdog (`main.js` + embedded PowerShell):** When the packaged auto-shutdown app starts on Windows, it spawns a detached PowerShell watchdog (`ramses-watchdog-*.ps1` in `%TEMP%`) and silently registers a user-scope `ONLOGON` scheduled task (`RamsesAutoShutdownLaunch`). The watchdog polls every 5 seconds; if `Ramses Auto Shutdown.exe` is not running, it relaunches it. The logon task re-arms everything at every Windows logon. A `data/admin-stopped.flag` sentinel file is written when the admin clicks "Stop App" — the watchdog consumes the sentinel and exits cleanly so admin-initiated shutdowns are respected (until the next logon). A `data/watchdog.lock` PID file prevents multiple concurrent watchdogs. All watchdog activity is logged to `data/watchdog.log` (rotated at 512 KB). No external scripts or installers required — protection is fully baked into the build.
39:- **Cross-App Mutual Exclusion (`src/app-lock.js`):** Both Electron entry points (`main.js` for auto-shutdown, `main-server.js` for Ramses Points) acquire a shared loopback TCP lock on `127.0.0.1:47318` at startup. Whichever app starts first wins; the second app queries the holder's role via `GET /ramses-role` and shows a friendly error dialog ("Cannot start: Ramses Points is already running on this PC…") then exits. This prevents the two apps from running on the same PC regardless of which port their HTTP servers use. The lock port is configurable via `RAMSES_LOCK_PORT`.
47:- **Read-Only Coin Logs:** Client apps can view coin logs and points but cannot modify them; modifications are restricted to the server-only `Ramses Points` application.
48:- **Ramses Points (Server-Only):** A lightweight Electron app running as a system tray icon, providing a central point for managing coin logs and rates for multiple clients.

